+# Matched five-layer replay: local candidate
+
+The fixed candidate reuses the three saved run20260930T113335113338Z terminals. It changes neither writer nor receiver. A user-run FP32 VAE child will decode each terminal once and retain the full clamped float and Q8 raster, then form matched first and second MP4s from that same chain. All four re-encodes consume181 complete frames; the unchanged reader uses common regular1..44 at fixed g0. The earlier terminal R45 result is not merged into these ranks.
+
+Fixed primary output is15normalized,30path/payload raw,5220valid costs plus all117450catalog/112230excluded slots,30path posthoc and60message evaluations. The call plan is0Transformer/3decode/12encode/6MP4save/6MP4read. Preclamp statistics, all46latent steps and raw local projections are retained. The original FULL.phase0 tensor/raw and original source/FULL hashes are separate historical references. Their absence does not fail the primary chain; whole-package/reference status stays explicit.
+
+Canonical result commits precede the recoverable blind projection. Model load failure preserves independently scored terminals; float encode failure does not prevent Q8 or matched media. Fresh-child monitoring terminates/waits before loading the latest canonical result. The output directory is refused if it resolves into the read-only input run. Raw commits precede truth joins. Posthoc records original-tolerance true rank/ties, unique top/path-start/false-edit facts and each layer's own winner, plus the same hash-bound original FULL.phase0 opponent across layers. Neither fixed opponents nor truth select a new path.
+
+Validation: first run11passed,0skip in12.57s. Its pytest stdout is preserved; only the surrounding shell's trailing exit-variable quoting failed after pytest completed. After a receipt-only runtime addition and a stronger extra-row test, the two affected tests passed in6.23s (9deselected). The full suite was not rerun. Both actual stdout files and execution receipts are included. All VAE/codec calls in these tests are mocks or lightweight fake classes using full geometry; original infer/family and quantizer are exercised. No real VAE/model/codec, GPU, Colab or saved-run ranking was executed by A1.
+
+Main independently produced the separate saved-terminal R44 baseline at /home/richar/projects/Video-WM/diagnostics/zero-mean-transfer-main-review-20260930/terminal_r44_baseline.json (SHA8144a1f5101c1bd1404b4bac4d624d5319f0a766e25f757d32d27d1b61d863d4). It reports6conditions/1044cost and OVERLAP/CORRECT true uniquely top among174, cost0.00023118449798124893, gap1.7460808162387176e-6. This is independent existing-input CPU evidence, not the new matched transfer experiment and not a rerun by A1.
+
+The new notebook is notebooks/zero_mean_c1_layered_transport_v1_colab.ipynb, with SOURCE_SHA=None. Its6cells/AST/Drive-first-cell/empty outputs/currentPython/Torch-pair probe/fresh child/dependency paths and builder identity were checked. It is an unpublished candidate, not a usable published Colab link. New source must be reviewed, published and immutably bound before the user executes it.
+
+No old tracked files or frozen design bytes changed. No source commit or push was made. Primary history and package completeness are separate from scientific conclusions. All scores remain uncalibrated and unaccepted; g0 is fixed, not recovered. The float layer is decode+mapping+clamp+encode, and the new decode need not reproduce the unavailable historical float buffer bitwise. No crop/four-phase matrix, C2, new watermark, threshold, ranking rule or quality gate was added.
